    "summary": "Legendary Capitol show with soaring Dark Star and tight jams",
    "blurb": "The set erupts from a blistering Not Fade Away into an otherworldly Dark Star, then rolls through Attics Of My Life into Sugar Magnolia and Saint Stephen. Jerry’s incendiary lead work and Phil’s locked‑in bass drive a seamless, psychedelic flow that Deadheads still cite as one of ’70’s finest.",
    "review": "Port Chester’s Capitol Theater on June 24, 1970 delivered what many fans still call a quintessential early‑’70 performance. The night opened with an acoustic first set before the band launched into a high‑energy second set where Not Fade Away became a launchpad for a soaring Dark Star that seemed to lift the entire house. From there the group chased each other through Attics Of My Life, another Dark Star, and a jubilant Sugar Magnolia before slipping into a tight Saint Stephen segueed into China Cat Sunflower and I Know You Rider. The encore closed with Uncle John’s Band and a heartfelt Swing Low, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all available tapes the show is praised for its seamless psychedelic transitions, blistering rhythm section, and Jerry Garcia’s “other‑worldly” lead work that still feels fresh today.",
